**TypeORM version:**

[x] `latest`
[ ] `@next`
[ ] `0.x.x` (or put your version here)

**Steps to reproduce or a small repository showing the problem:**

I have two fields within my entity that have _nullable_ set to _false_, which will set the field null during an update (both in the relation and column).

```ts
@Entity('Account')
export class AccountEntity {

    @ManyToOne(type => RecordTypeEntity, {
        nullable: false
    })
    @JoinColumn({ name: 'RecordTypeId' })
    recordType: RecordTypeEntity;

    @Column({
        name: 'Phone',
        type: 'varchar',
        nullable: false
    })
    phone: string;
}
```

However, when running (I'm showing the Jest test I have it in), setting the fields to null will set them null in the database during the update, and the test will fail. **This does happen in the running server, I'm just showing the test because it's more concise.**

```ts
return AccountEntity.save(account).then(() => {
    return AccountEntity.findOneById(account.sfid, {
        join: {
            alias: 'account',
            innerJoinAndSelect: {
                'recordType': 'account.recordType'
            }
        }
    }).then(result => {

        result.phone = null;
        result.recordType = null;

        return AccountEntity.save(result).then(() => {
            return AccountEntity.findOneById(account.sfid, {
                join: {
                    alias: 'account',
                    innerJoinAndSelect: {
                        'recordType': 'account.recordType'
                    }
                }
            }).then(result => {

                expect(result).toBeDefined();

                expect(result.recordType).toEqual(account.recordType);
                expect(result.phone).toEqual(account.phone);

            });
        });

    });

});
```

This is spit out in the logs during the test - so you can see that it's updating the field.

```console
console.log node_modules/typeorm/platform/PlatformTools.js:207
executing query:  START TRANSACTION

console.log node_modules/typeorm/platform/PlatformTools.js:207
executing query:  UPDATE `Account` SET `Phone`=?, `RecordTypeId`=?  WHERE `Id`=? -- PARAMETERS: [null,null,"1e6ecbc2-6890-44bd"]

console.log node_modules/typeorm/platform/PlatformTools.js:207
executing query:  COMMIT
```

The only way I can get it to work is to set the fields to undefined instead of null

```ts
result.phone = undefined;
result.recordType = undefined;
```


